1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Maya-style project
Create, Set, Open scene, Save as, workspace.mel

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.883
The project system mirrors Maya's Set Project: a folder holding scenes, sourceimages, images and the rest, and a workspace.mel that Maya recognises.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:14.317
Create: pick where and what to call it. Landfall builds the folders, writes the workspace.mel and makes the project current.

4
00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:19.750
The current project's name appears at the top of the section. Set makes an existing project current, one made by Maya too.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.183
Open scene, or Ctrl+O, opens the browser straight inside scenes/. With no project it is Blender's Open.

6
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.617
Save as, or Ctrl+Shift+S, saves into scenes/ with relative paths. A file already in the project stays where it is. Ctrl+S overwrites the current file, as in Blender.

7
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:36.050
Before moving or copying the project, Make paths relative. Write workspace.mel adds Maya's file to a project made without one.

8
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.483
In the preferences: the projects' root folder, renders in images/, the assets/ folder as an asset library.

9
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:44.417
Project

